       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. 1600 mg four times daily comes to 6,400 mg/day. That is double the maximum daily ibuprofen dose for adults, which is 3,200 mg/day under supervised use. Over-the-counter use is capped at 1,200 mg/day. A dose this high raises the risk of GI bleeding, kidney injury, and cardiovascular events.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **400 mg PO four times daily**, which is 1,600 mg/day.\n- **800 mg PO three times daily**, which is 2,400 mg/day. This is a common anti-inflammatory regimen.\n- **800 mg PO four times daily**, which is 3,200 mg/day. This is the maximum.\n- **1600 mg/day total**, divided into a different schedule.\n\nTell me the dose and frequency you want and I'll enter it right away. If you do want 1600 mg four times daily, please confirm that explicitly. I'd also like to add a note with the rationale to the order."
